What would make me admit the thesis is getting weaker

I want this recorded now because otherwise almost any future outcome can be rationalized.

I would reduce conviction materially if several of these happen:

Google puts Gemini on many products but the underlying context and task state remain siloed.

Watches, glasses, cars and laptops get separate Gemini interfaces but little real continuity between them.

Personal context produces noise rather than meaningfully better decisions.

Search usage rises but monetization deteriorates structurally.

A2A becomes important while Google captures little value from hosting, identity, security, governance or execution.

Agent Registry remains peripheral.

Another AI company becomes the main user-facing layer on Android or Chrome while Google becomes a replaceable backend.

CapEx stays extremely high for years without a corresponding increase in normalized free cash flow.

Robotics remains technically impressive but strategically isolated from the rest of the Google stack.

Regulation prevents Google from connecting the parts of the ecosystem that matter most.

None of these alone automatically destroys the thesis.

But if several happen together, the graph I am betting on is not forming the way I expect.

